#{[{:activity/_scope [{:activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134619} :activity/id #uuid "28765c46-c394-55b1-842f-82e4066f9786" :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134619 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186135028 :tutorial/content "To construct the standard matrix of a linear transformation $T$ in $\\mathbb{R}^2,$ we find the images of the vectors in the standard basis $\\{ \\mathbf{i}, \\mathbf{j} \\}$ of $\\mathbb{R}^2$ under $T,$ and then use those images as columns in the standard matrix.\n\nTo demonstrate, let's consider the following linear transformation: \n\n![](images/b3/b399f02949935d4a4425b19e4946a3eb47375272bb0271586c93da504ff0bd2e.svg)\n\nComputing $\\mathbf T(\\mathbf i),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(i) & =T\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2\\cdot 1-1\\cdot 0 \\\\ 1+3\\cdot 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing $\\mathbf T(\\mathbf j),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(j) & =T\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2\\cdot 0-1\\cdot 1 \\\\ 0+3\\cdot 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the standard matrix for this linear transformation is ![](images/be/be0afb6703a6d5e4bcbb360297240a74f4aeec7efbbb1229c8cd01e112fa6bda.svg)\n\nIn the diagram below, we see the vectors in the standard basis $\\{ \\mathbf{i}, \\mathbf{j} \\}$ of $\\mathbb{R}^2$ and their images $\\{ \\mathbf{i'}, \\mathbf{j'} \\}$ under the transformation.\n\n![](images/91/9189a79fe44936221e38e7c051f9f0ddd53338c80cd324ba804d61beef6c2c44.png)\n\nIn general, a linear transformation in $\\mathbb R^n$ has a standard matrix of dimensions $n \\times n,$ whose columns are the images of the basis vectors under the action of the linear transformation." :tutorial/id #uuid "840f3f2c-df1b-50e6-afae-b6c5a434f7a5" :tutorial/math-academy-id 3528 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "5711f04c-b960-52c7-925d-15098acb82c7" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134622}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134620 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133754 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bca46ab2-488a-5596-b96b-559463731556"} :step/id #uuid "b4fbcf6d-62ba-54b7-9625-c8521044b1e0"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134621 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133755 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a2845913-5c76-57f5-a4d3-139a6513225b"} :step/id #uuid "ec1bcfe7-e63e-5e9f-a750-0f39702b4059" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134620}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134622 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133756 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b057dd5e-f80e-5d3f-84ae-b6aebd5800ea"} :step/id #uuid "985fd7a6-d14e-5ae5-9b05-95876d3e50f2" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134621}}] :activity/title "The Standard Matrix of a Linear Transformation in Terms of the Standard Basis" :activity/type {:db/ident :activity.type/lesson} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186134047}] :db/id #edb/ref 17592186048326 :topic/knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133754 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133563 :question/id #uuid "4748324b-8edf-5fba-90e1-90683887d463" :question/math-academy-id "e-5436" :question/problem "The linear transformation $\\mathbf T$ has the standard matrix \n![](images/6a/6a14933078db8802426a1ab22ba692e17fd6f795ec4bd746a6fb16687aa441ed.svg) \nWhat are the images of the standard basis vectors $\\{ \\mathbf{i}, \\mathbf{j} \\}$ of $\\mathbb{R}^2$ under the action of $\\mathbf T?$" :question/worked-solution "**Method 1**\n\nThe images of the vectors in the standard basis $\\{ \\mathbf{i}, \\mathbf{j} \\}$ are the first and second columns of $T,$ respectively. \n\nTherefore, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(i) & =T\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 8\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ T(j) & =T\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nWe can find the images of the vectors in the standard basis $\\{ \\mathbf{i}, \\mathbf{j} \\}$ by computing the matrix products $T\\cdot\\mathbf{i}$ and $T\\cdot\\mathbf{j}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(i) & =T\\cdot i=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 5 \\\\ 8 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 8\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ T(j) & =T\\cdot j=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 5 \\\\ 8 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bca46ab2-488a-5596-b96b-559463731556" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134428 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "02074b21-6e5f-5e2e-ba73-59a993b60196" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}$,\n$\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}$, \n and $\\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476205} {:answer/id #uuid "5af4cee8-bacc-5e67-b48a-fde6ecdf72fb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 8\\end{bmatrix}$,\n$\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$, \n and $\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476404} {:answer/id #uuid "d8ca38df-97cf-5200-bfc8-99ef358d6607" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}$,\n$\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}$, \n and $\\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476694} {:answer/id #uuid "e9349e04-0095-5d5e-8eb3-f1e19c418f89" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 8 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}$,\n$\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$, \n and $\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476722} {:answer/id #uuid "f8695bb3-3962-5bb5-9f2d-b70827e500e7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 8\\end{bmatrix}$,\n$\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}$, \n and $\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476750}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 8\\end{bmatrix}$,\n$\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}$, \n and $\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476750} :answer-field/id #uuid "a9fba76a-fa1f-56f3-a156-563fef2e304a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132607}] :question/id #uuid "34b068e8-ab54-5792-afa1-011595ad4802" :question/math-academy-id "q-43890" :question/problem "The linear transformation $T$ has the standard matrix \n\n$$\nT=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 1 & -5 \\\\ 8 & -1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhat are the respective images of the standard basis vectors $\\{i,j,k\\}$ of ${R}^{3}$ under the action of $T?$" :question/worked-solution "**Method 1**\n\nThe images of the vectors in the standard basis $\\{i,j,k\\}$ are the first, second, and third columns of $T,$ respectively. \n\nTherefore, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(i) & =T\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 8\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ T(j) & =T\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ T(k) & =T\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nWe can find the images of the vectors in the standard basis $\\{i,j,k\\}$ by computing the matrix products $T\\cdot i,$ $T\\cdot j,$ and $T\\cdot k:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(i) & =T\\cdot i=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 1 & -5 \\\\ 8 & -1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 8\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ T(j) & =T\\cdot j=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 1 & -5 \\\\ 8 & -1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ T(k) & =T\\cdot k=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 1 & -5 \\\\ 8 & -1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134430 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "38025c76-7296-51ce-b26c-f8e7311afc56" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$ and $\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476328} {:answer/id #uuid "51d82f90-9a22-5286-ad37-3dac355225c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}$ and $\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476376} {:answer/id #uuid "6fbe14ec-f5b8-5b17-b0f7-8b51c052798d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}$ and $\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476452} {:answer/id #uuid "c167f295-c000-56a8-a353-b451577aa310" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$ and $\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476640} {:answer/id #uuid "e498fa1c-b1fb-500f-a040-f84da4313219" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}$ and $\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476711}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}$ and $\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476711} :answer-field/id #uuid "086168dd-27ed-5da8-8056-ad16a2b501b0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132619}] :question/id #uuid "655dd154-95c9-5f77-bf5c-6a9ca9818844" :question/math-academy-id "q-43893" :question/problem "The linear transformation $T$ has the standard matrix \n\n$$\nT=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & -4 \\\\ 5 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n \nWhat are the respective images of the standard basis vectors $\\{i,j\\}$ of ${R}^{2}$ under the action of $T?$" :question/worked-solution "**Method 1**\n\nThe images of the vectors in the standard basis $\\{i,j\\}$ are the first and second columns of $T,$ respectively. \n\nTherefore, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(i) & =T\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ T(j) & =T\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nWe can find the images of the vectors in the standard basis $\\{i,j\\}$ by computing the matrix products $T\\cdot i$ and $T\\cdot j:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(i) & =T\\cdot i=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & -4 \\\\ 5 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ T(j) & =T\\cdot j=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & -4 \\\\ 5 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186271997 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1158612a-a7cd-5401-ab01-884881dbd8d2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}$ and $\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269424} {:answer/id #uuid "25796603-b8ef-53b2-90f1-f9c959e51ec7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$ and $\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269601} {:answer/id #uuid "3712d637-fa08-572c-9e76-d35ca80a41bd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}$ and $\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269767} {:answer/id #uuid "6d7317fe-4f7e-5a1f-be6b-2f5996d768e0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}$ and $\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270241} {:answer/id #uuid "85756b75-8e0f-5102-aaa1-aafda8c11e44" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}$ and $\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270422}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}$ and $\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269424} :answer-field/id #uuid "148da24d-b545-5cb2-8bb3-9e2e120371a7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271544}] :question/id #uuid "c4ba68e0-97ab-529f-b81d-0c51ba604b51" :question/math-academy-id "q-139993" :question/problem "The linear transformation $T$ has the standard matrix \n\n$$\nT=\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n \nWhat are the respective images of the standard basis vectors ${i,j}$ of ${R}^{2}$ under the action of $T?$" :question/worked-solution "**Method 1**\n\nThe images of the vectors in the standard basis ${i,j}$ are the first and second columns of $T,$ respectively. \n\nTherefore, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(i) & =T\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ T(j) & =T\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nWe can find the images of the vectors in the standard basis ${i,j}$ by computing the matrix products $T\\cdot i$ and $T\\cdot j:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(i) & =T\\cdot i=\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ T(j) & =T\\cdot j=\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329741 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "65117d9d-ac17-5c3c-ad23-40504ec9738e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$ and $\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327814} {:answer/id #uuid "6fe2c1bf-0d41-5bd6-852b-bcb47dca1f2a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}$ and $\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327906} {:answer/id #uuid "a36a262a-8e9c-5530-80c7-c4dcef50c604" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}$ and $\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328346} {:answer/id #uuid "c69e47ae-8ddc-53a7-bcd5-6cfe3241a999" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}$ and $\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328681} {:answer/id #uuid "cad333f1-fc80-560c-a3ad-32d711fb17e2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}$ and $\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328710}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$ and $\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327814} :answer-field/id #uuid "f23c2ed0-a69d-5485-9217-a853a3ba817c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329605}] :question/id #uuid "36e3ad83-f361-5d68-9744-a8a366bc0803" :question/math-academy-id "q-43836" :question/problem "The linear transformation $T$ has the standard matrix \n\n$$\nT=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n \nWhat are the respective images of the standard basis vectors ${i,j}$ of ${R}^{2}$ under the action of $T?$" :question/worked-solution "**Method 1**\n\nThe images of the vectors in the standard basis ${i,j}$ are the first and second columns of $T,$ respectively. \n\nTherefore, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(i) & =T\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ T(j) & =T\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nWe can find the images of the vectors in the standard basis ${i,j}$ by computing the matrix products $T\\cdot i$ and $T\\cdot j:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(i) & =T\\cdot i=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ T(j) & =T\\cdot j=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348052 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3a497af5-5eb9-56bf-b12d-3f387cd8a6f3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}$, $\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}$, and $\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345848} {:answer/id #uuid "4637f099-4ee7-5d9e-9432-c575e089e8ea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}$, $\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}$, and $\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345963} {:answer/id #uuid "974b41e6-8824-5a0e-8dfe-a667359d08c5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}$, $\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}$, and $\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346675} {:answer/id #uuid "d2617b0d-86a5-53d1-