swer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+6{R}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552159} :answer-field/id #uuid "2d0a791f-68bf-567b-9398-0225c9085e8f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552278}] :question/id #uuid "697a3132-99c3-5286-b927-185afe5caf9e" :question/math-academy-id "q-75076" :question/problem "Let $E=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].$ Find the row operation that, when applied to a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A,$ gives the result of the product $EA.$" :question/worked-solution "The matrix $E$ is obtained by taking the first row of the identity matrix and adding $6$ times the second row:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+6{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =E\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $EA$ is equivalent to applying the row operation ${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+6{R}_{2}$ to $A.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186552453 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "244dda5b-5b90-5880-91d6-8964f79bd7d8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{2}:=-2{R}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551747} {:answer/id #uuid "58869cfc-79d4-5f7b-b6a1-25e2a3bbe897" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551877} {:answer/id #uuid "6c0a9f51-e34e-59e8-939a-0f36ea7dc858" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{2}:=-2{R}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551916} {:answer/id #uuid "875518a0-30c3-54be-b6df-66fbc1c064d8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{2}:=2{R}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551993} {:answer/id #uuid "8e4aad5e-10a6-5e44-a3de-51d162a2df8d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+(-2){R}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552012}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{2}:=-2{R}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551747} :answer-field/id #uuid "89a3a7d4-f7bf-5719-83a5-a5301c0b7f61" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552334}] :question/id #uuid "6f2a6c54-ca8b-593a-b61e-5ecaccecd8e7" :question/math-academy-id "q-32010" :question/problem "Let $E=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}].$ Find the row operation that, when applied to a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A,$ gives the result of the product $EA.$" :question/worked-solution "The given matrix $E$ is obtained by multiplying the second row of the identity matrix by $-2$: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=-2{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =E\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $EA$ is equivalent to applying the row operation  ${R}_{2}:=-2{R}_{2}$ to $A.$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Row Operation That's Equivalent To Left Multiplication by an Elementary Matrix"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115247 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115076 :question/id #uuid "9927d1a6-a119-5987-9f49-5171a3f2e2d3" :question/math-academy-id "e-4721" :question/problem "Suppose we are applying the elementary row operation $R_1:=R_1 - R_2$ to a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A.$ Find the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication." :question/worked-solution "We need to find an elementary matrix $E$ such that $EA$ is equivalent to applying the elementary row operation $R_1:=R_1 - R_2$ to $A.$\n\nTo find $E,$ we apply the given row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}-{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =E\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication is $EA\\mathbin{:}$\n![](images/11/11c345fde8fecb2e2a5459a0868ad8892e9067820de72f91601c1033858ca019.svg)"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "94c2cd65-810b-52ad-a20d-7b5a0a9eaf2b" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115741 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "14409a4e-e639-5c85-a959-813bcf39866a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "A\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551706} {:answer/id #uuid "2c15976c-5217-554b-b5e6-25f340bb4cb1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551768} {:answer/id #uuid "4309dd5e-648e-5748-8db9-6912a5b72563" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551826} {:answer/id #uuid "5f29dc8a-4c28-5af7-93ea-28714a404c42" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551895} {:answer/id #uuid "7d89f0f0-b54b-5f94-a76d-2254fc112b9d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "A\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551964}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551768} :answer-field/id #uuid "f3cbf19e-29ab-5677-9980-cb6d9925144c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113412}] :question/id #uuid "a384818e-7ec3-5e40-9b82-69307830196b" :question/math-academy-id "q-32039" :question/problem "Suppose we are applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+4{R}_{2}$ to a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A.$ Find the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication." :question/worked-solution "We need to find an elementary matrix $E$ such that $EA$ is equivalent to applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+4{R}_{2}$ to $A.$\n\nTo find $E,$ we apply the given row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+4{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =E\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication is $EA:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115845 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9db86be4-e9a5-5ab9-b290-aa3d8453a260" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "A \\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186114008} {:answer/id #uuid "d70a14e7-6fca-5454-bd01-e970ab20a237" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "A \\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{4} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186114009} {:answer/id #uuid "e4ea65b9-1980-573a-a034-55d7bf4b1d08" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{4} & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186114010} {:answer/id #uuid "17ec4bea-53d3-52ee-a166-bfe2b2f35049" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "A \\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -\\frac{1}{4}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186114011} {:answer/id #uuid "4ff76435-c6d5-5886-af1f-b8bb592c0289" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{4} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186114012}] :answer-field/id #uuid "4a0fc896-b7c3-50d1-9440-7943399cd45e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186114007}] :question/id #uuid "bf275abe-7363-5683-96de-adaf02f1ed3e" :question/math-academy-id "q-42810" :question/problem "Suppose we are applying the elementary row operati