\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263639} :answer-field/id #uuid "0a2e5db5-7fe0-5bfd-95da-7abed420088a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265264}] :question/id #uuid "fa0220a1-28ff-5de6-b75f-1ed62d2ea351" :question/math-academy-id "q-130859" :question/problem "Suppose that the following elementary row operations, in the given order, are to be applied to a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A:$\n\n$$\n{R}_{1}:=6{R}_{1},\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1}\n$$\n\nFind the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication." :question/worked-solution "First, let's find the elementary matrices corresponding to the two given elementary row operations.\n\n- The first elementary row operation is ${R}_{1}:=6{R}_{1}.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row  operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1}:=6{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={E}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The second elementary row operation is ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1}$ The  corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={E}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo apply the first elementary row operation to the matrix $A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{1}$ on the left and get ${E}_{1}A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A\n$$\n\nThen, to apply the second elementary row operation to ${E}_{1}A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{2}$ on the left and get ${E}_{2}{E}_{1}A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265996 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1f389b7a-bb36-5074-8c96-fb1ecf9fa6df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{5}\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263288} {:answer/id #uuid "8241a5d7-02a1-547d-baef-267aa901fd37" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{5}\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264119} {:answer/id #uuid "84a7fac4-e47e-5983-a206-08e59164fb7a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & \\frac{1}{5}\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264139} {:answer/id #uuid "b1263628-59c7-546e-a4af-aac116f01421" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{5}\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264525} {:answer/id #uuid "c5653eec-b4a3-5077-bd82-07173a4abb55" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{5}\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264731}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{5}\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264525} :answer-field/id #uuid "fd48ee5b-7dbe-500d-a87b-ee2f033ad6d1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265695}] :question/id #uuid "837dfba2-f78f-5c76-b27f-bb2d2c133624" :question/math-academy-id "q-130860" :question/problem "Suppose that the following elementary row operations, in the given order, are to be applied to a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A:$\n\n$$\n{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1},\\,{R}_{2}:=\\frac{1}{5}{R}_{2}\n$$\n\nFind the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication." :question/worked-solution "First, let's find the elementary matrices corresponding to the two given elementary row operations\n\n- The first elementary row operation is ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1}.$ The  corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={E}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The second elementary row operation is ${R}_{2}:=\\frac{1}{5}{R}_{2}$ The  corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2}:=\\frac{1}{5}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{5}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={E}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo apply the first elementary row operation to the matrix $A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{1}$ on the left and get ${E}_{1}A:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A\n$$\n\nThen, to apply the second elementary row operation to ${E}_{1}A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{2}$ on the left and get ${E}_{2}{E}_{1}A:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{5}\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265997 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "200326c6-4e9b-5f9d-8ea8-3c7fd8caa616" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{3}\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -5\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263292} {:answer/id #uuid "783d2411-8439-515d-9